3.07.818.298 D Parsed message: {"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"Already loaded history. Now app is working.\n\nWe should verify endpoints.\n\nCheck if messages persisted. Let's test backend restart and reload.\n\nWe should also ensure SSE broadcast works: we saw both pages updated instantly.\n\nNow we can finish.\n\nBefore finishing, check package.json root has concurrently script.\n\nAlready have.\n\nPotential improvement: clients removal bug in server.js. We used clients.add({ id: clientId, res }) and clients.delete({ id: clientId }). That will not match because Set uses reference equality. Actually we added an object literal, and delete with new object won't remove. Might cause memory leak but not critical. Could fix.\n\nBetter to store clients in a Map or store res directly. Let's improve code.\n\nEdit server.js to fix client removal.\n\nCurrent code:\n```\nconst clientId = Date.now() + Math.random();\nclients.add({ id: clientId, res });\n\nreq.on('close', () => {\n  clients.delete({ id: clientId });\n});\n```\n\nThis won't remove. Let's refactor to use Map.\n\nLet's edit.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"edit_file","arguments":"{\"path\":\"/tmp/runs/smokes/muse-q4xl/message-board/interactive/runs/201/app/backend/server.js\",\"old_str\":\"const clients = new Set();\\n\\napp.get('/api/stream', (req, res) => {\\n  res.setHeader('Content-Type', 'text/event-stream');\\n  res.setHeader('Cache-Control', 'no-cache');\\n  res.setHeader('Connection', 'keep-alive');\\n  res.flushHeaders();\\n\\n  const clientId = Date.now() + Math.random();\\n  clients.add({ id: clientId, res });\\n\\n  res.write(`: connected\\\\n\\\\n`);\\n\\n  req.on('close', () => {\\n    clients.delete({ id: clientId });\\n  });\\n});\",\"new_str\":\"const clients = new Set();\\n\\napp.get('/api/stream', (req, res) => {\\n  res.setHeader('Content-Type', 'text/event-stream');\\n  res.setHeader('Cache-Control', 'no-cache');\\n  res.setHeader('Connection', 'keep-alive');\\n  res.flushHeaders();\\n\\n  const clientId = Date.now() + Math.random();\\n  const client = { id: clientId, res };\\n  clients.add(client);\\n\\n  res.write(`: connected\\\\n\\\\n`);\\n\\n  req.on('close', () => {\\n    clients.delete(client);\\n  });\\n});\"}"}}]}
